		<profileDesc>
			<abstract>
				<p>Large Language Models (LLMs) have significantly advanced legal intelligence, but the scarcity of scenario data impedes the progress toward interactive legal scenarios. This paper introduces a Multi-agent Legal Simulation Driver (MASER) to scalably generate synthetic data by simulating interactive legal scenarios. Leveraging real-legal case sources, MASER ensures the consistency of legal attributes between participants and introduces a supervisory mechanism to align participants&apos; characters and behaviors as well as addressing distractions. A Multi-stage Interactive Legal Evaluation (MILE) benchmark is further constructed to evaluate LLMs&apos; performance in dynamic legal scenarios. Extensive experiments confirm the effectiveness of our framework. The detailed resources are available at https://github.com/FudanDISC/MASER.</p>
			</abstract>
		</profileDesc>
